          "name": "Bombycilla garrulus",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Bohemian waxwing",
          "lineage": "Waxwings",
          "continents": [
            "Europe",
            "North America"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 2,
          "description": "The Bohemian waxwing is a starling-sized passerine bird that breeds in the northern forests of the Palearctic and North America. It has mainly buff-grey plumage, black face markings and a pointed crest. Its wings are patterned with white and bright yellow, and some of the wing feathers have red tips, the resemblance of which to sealing wax gives these birds their common name.",
